{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pulls/1","id":3681670552,"node_id":"PR_kwDOR6Um6s7bcdWY","html_url":"https://github.com/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/issues/1","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"feat: admin auth, request observability, header standardization, policy lifecycle","user":{"login":"vickky06","id":51980219,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUxOTgwMjE5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/51980219?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06","html_url":"https://github.com/vickky06","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/vickky06/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"## **User description**\nfeat: admin auth, request observability, header standardization, policy lifecycle\n\n- Gate /admin/clients/{id}/strategy behind a shared admin key (X-Admin-Key)\n  so only platform operators with the build-time secret can rotate policies.\n- Per-request log line in RateLimit middleware (method, URL, headers) for\n  SRE to trace throttling decisions back to originating callers.\n- Rename ClientIDHeader from X-API-Key to X-Client-ID to match the platform\n  convention now used across the gateway services.\n- Tighten SlidingWindow boundary: requests landing exactly at the configured\n  limit now block instead of squeezing through.\n- Per-policy window-monitor goroutine on UpdateLimiter so operators can\n  inspect window-rotation cadence post-rotation.\n- Best-effort UpdateLimiter and NewClientStore: invalid policies are logged\n  and skipped rather than failing the whole admin call or boot.\n\n\n___\n\n## **CodeAnt-AI Description**\n**Tighten rate limiting and add admin protection for policy updates**\n\n### What Changed\n- Admin policy updates now require the shared admin key, so only approved operators can change client rules\n- Rate-limit requests are logged with method, URL, and headers to make throttling decisions easier to trace\n- Client identity now uses the new `X-Client-ID` header across the gateway\n- Sliding window limits now block requests that land exactly at the limit instead of letting them through\n- Invalid client policies are skipped instead of stopping startup or blocking an admin update\n- Updated coverage for rate limiting behavior, header handling, quota denial, health checks, and strategy calculations\n\n### Impact\n`✅ Safer policy changes`\n`✅ Clearer throttling traces`\n`✅ Fewer boundary-limit bypasses`\n\n\n[🔄 Retrigger CodeAnt AI Review](https://api.codeant.ai/pr/retrigger_review?id=sE-4yvknFU4MeJuxs2RZVcLMgIDrI3-XQtQYa2Pu2Es&org=vickky06)<details><summary><strong>💡 Usage Guide</strong></summary>\n\n### Checking Your Pull Request\nEvery time you make a pull request, our system automatically looks through it. We check for security issues, mistakes in how you're setting up your infrastructure, and common code problems. We do this to make sure your changes are solid and won't cause any trouble later.\n\n### Talking to CodeAnt AI\nGot a question or need a hand with something in your pull request? You can easily get in touch with CodeAnt AI right here. Just type the following in a comment on your pull request, and replace \"Your question here\" with whatever you want to ask:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Your question here</code>\n</pre>\nThis lets you have a chat with CodeAnt AI about your pull request, making it easier to understand and improve your code.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai ask: Can you suggest a safer alternative to storing this secret?</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Preserve Org Learnings with CodeAnt\nYou can record team preferences so CodeAnt AI applies them in future reviews. Reply directly to the specific CodeAnt AI suggestion (in the same thread) and replace \"Your feedback here\" with your input:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Your feedback here</code>\n</pre>\nThis helps CodeAnt AI learn and adapt to your team's coding style and standards.\n\n#### Example\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: Do not flag unused imports.</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Retrigger review\nAsk CodeAnt AI to review the PR again, by typing:\n<pre>\n<code>@codeant-ai: review</code>\n</pre>\n\n### Check Your Repository Health\nTo analyze the health of your code repository, visit our dashboard at [https://app.codeant.ai](https://app.codeant.ai). This tool helps you identify potential issues and areas for improvement in your codebase, ensuring your repository maintains high standards of code health.\n\n</details>\n","created_at":"2026-05-14T08:43:19Z","updated_at":"2026-05-14T08:47:55Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"6b609a30c9cc2fd5fd4e7f1896a8deff8cbf672e","assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"labels":[{"id":10949703961,"node_id":"LA_kwDOR6Um6s8AAAACjKc5GQ","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/labels/size:L","name":"size:L","color":"bfd4f2","default":false,"description":"This PR changes 100-499 lines, ignoring generated files"}],"milestone":null,"draft":false,"commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vickky06/Rate-Limiter/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://a